# ── Supabase (the whole app, not just /admin) ─────────────────────────────────
#
# This header used to say "Required only for the /admin/* routes" and "the
# customer app uses localStorage and never reads these". Both were true in
# Phase 1 and are not true now: auth, cloud sync and every public token page
# (RSVP, invitation, gift, album, hostess, collab) read Supabase, and so does
# the Netlify edge function that renders the OG tags for /invite/*. Without
# these two the customer app has no login and no sync at all.
#
# localStorage is still the source of truth — Supabase is the second copy.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Create a project at https://supabase.com
#   2. Copy Project URL and anon/public key from:
#      Project Settings → API → Project URL / Project API Keys
#   3. Create this file as .env.local (gitignored) with your real values:
#      cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Create the first admin user:
#   Run in Supabase SQL editor or Dashboard → Authentication → Users:
#   (any user you create manually can log in — no self-registration is exposed)
#
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ── Stripe (client-side — safe to expose) ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# STATUS: BUILT, NOT SWITCHED ON. This said "payment UI not wired up yet",
# which stopped being true some time ago. The Account screen renders the
# upgrade and billing-portal buttons, useBilling calls src/lib/stripe.js, and
# that invokes two live Edge Functions (create-checkout-session,
# create-billing-portal) with the webhook deployed. What is missing is the KEY:
# with this variable empty, `isStripeConfigured` is false and the UI hides
# itself. Pricing is frozen by the owner's decision, so it stays empty on
# purpose — that is a business decision, not an unbuilt feature.
#
# VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY   Stripe publishable key (pk_live_… or pk_test_…)
#                               Found in: Stripe Dashboard → Developers → API keys
#
VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ── Support contact (client-side — safe to expose) ────────────────────────────
#
# VITE_SUPPORT_WHATSAPP         Phone number for the floating support button,
#                               international format without "+" or spaces
#                               (e.g. 972501234567). Empty hides the button.
#
# VITE_SUPPORT_EMAIL            Address behind the "feedback" and "Enterprise
#                               inquiry" mailto links on the account screen.
#                               Was read in two places and documented in none;
#                               empty falls back to support@kochav-hashulchan.co.il,
#                               which is a domain that has to actually exist.
#
VITE_SUPPORT_WHATSAPP=
VITE_SUPPORT_EMAIL=

# ── Server-side only — Supabase Edge Function secrets ─────────────────────────
#
# These values must NEVER be added to VITE_ variables: anything with a VITE_
# prefix is compiled into the browser bundle.
#
# Set them via Supabase Dashboard → Edge Functions → Secrets, or:
#   supabase secrets set STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_…
#
# SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are injected
# by the Edge runtime automatically — listed here only so the list of what the
# functions read is complete. Everything below has to be set by hand.
#
# ── Billing (create-checkout-session, create-billing-portal, stripe-webhook)
#
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY             Stripe secret key (sk_live_… or sk_test_…)
#                               Found in: Stripe Dashboard → Developers → API keys
#
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET         Webhook signing secret (whsec_…)
#                               Found in: Stripe Dashboard → Developers → Webhooks
#                               → select your endpoint → Signing secret
#                               Required to verify all incoming webhook events.
#
# STRIPE_PRO_PRICE_ID           Stripe Price ID for the Pro plan (price_…)
#                               Create in: Stripe Dashboard → Products → Pro → Add price
#
# STRIPE_ENTERPRISE_PRICE_ID    Stripe Price ID for the Enterprise plan (price_…)
#                               Create in: Stripe Dashboard → Products → Enterprise → Add price
#
# APP_ORIGINS                   Comma-separated allow-list of origins the two
#                               billing functions accept CORS requests from.
#                               Both branch explicitly on it being unset.
#
# ── Floor-plan detection (detect-floor-plan)
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY             Key for the Claude call that reads a venue
#                               floor plan. The function is deployed and does
#                               nothing without it.
#
# ── Photo retention (purge-event-photos)
#
# PURGE_SECRET                  Shared secret the pg_cron job sends as the
#                               x-purge-secret header. The function refuses
#                               every request while it is unset — deliberately,
#                               so an unconfigured deploy cannot delete photos.
#
# Example (do not commit real values):
#   STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_…
#   STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_…
#   STRIPE_PRO_PRICE_ID=price_…
#   STRIPE_ENTERPRISE_PRICE_ID=price_…
#   APP_ORIGINS=https://kochav-hashulchan.co.il,http://localhost:5173
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-…
#   PURGE_SECRET=…

# ── Analytics — PostHog (client-side — safe to expose) ────────────────────────
#
# STATUS: dark until this is set. No key means no requests, no cookies and no
# consent question — which is how every developer machine and CI run stays
# silent without anyone remembering to make it so.
#
# Deliberately configured in src/lib/analytics.js with autocapture OFF, session
# recording OFF and posthog's own pageview OFF. Those are posthog defaults and
# each one leaks other people's data here: autocapture sends the text of the
# element clicked (a guest's name), and the automatic pageview sends the raw
# URL (nine public routes carry a token, which is a credential). Do not turn
# them on — src/lib/analytics.test.js fails if you do.
#
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=
# Defaults to https://eu.i.posthog.com — the EU region, so the data does not
# leave it. Only set this to override.
VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=
